15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing selection from the CORSIP cohort in British Columbia, with seventeen LC cases, twelve with specimens, split into transcriptomics \(eight cases, PAXgene samples, twenty-nine controls\) and metabolomics \(six cases with serum, six controls\), leading to network analysis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a principal component analysis \(PCA\) scatterplot comparing case \(blue\) and control \(orange\) groups, each with ellipses indicating group variance. Panel B is a volcano plot showing significant gene expression changes, with genes upregulated in cases \(orange\) or downregulated in cases \(blue\) labeled, including ANXA1, RPS6, S100A8, LY96, ITGA2B, CD163, THBS1, and KIR_Inhibiting_Subgroup_1.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Heatmap illustration shows Spearman correlation coefficients among six immune-related scores: Neutrophil_score, S100A8, NK_score, KIR_inhibitory_score, NK_function_score, and Cytotoxic_score. Positive correlations are red, negative are blue, with hierarchical clustering dendrograms at top and left. Color scale bar ranges from negative zero point four to one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a PCA plot with blue and yellow dots representing cases and controls, respectively, each enclosed by ellipses; axes are labeled PC1 and PC2 with variance explained. Panel B is a volcano plot displaying metabolites significantly upregulated or downregulated in cases versus controls, with dots color-coded and labeled metabolites highlighted; axes are Log2 fold change and negative Log10 P value. Legend explains dot colors and sample sizes.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Violin plots compare pre- and post-infection metabolite concentrations for control \(orange\) and case \(blue\) groups with individual participant values, showing statistically significant differences for oxoglutarate, deoxyuridine, threonine, oxoadipate, and 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate, as marked by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Network analysis visualization shows two panels: panel a displays a network map with blue and orange nodes representing transcriptomics and metabolomics data respectively, node size reflecting degree, and labeled protein names; panel b presents a dot plot of the top 20 KEGG enriched pathways, with dot size indicating number of hits and color gradient representing significance level measured by \205log10\(FDR\), highlighting serotoninergic synapse and necroptosis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
